<tr><td colspan="2">The <CFOUTPUT>#application.returned_customer_setting.Trade_Label# #Application.PlannerLabel# helps users plan trade programs for #application.returned_customer_setting.distributor_label_plural#.</CFOUTPUT></td></tr>

<tr><td valign="top"> <img src="../../images/1.gif"></td><td>
You can make a new trade plan by clicking on [create] or show existing ones by clicking on [list].
</td></tr>
<tr><td valign="top"> <img src="../../images/2.gif">  </td><td>
<cfoutput>The Report Title and Notes are what was entered when the plan was created. You can change the #application.returned_customer_setting.distributor_label_singular# by clicking on the [change #application.returned_customer_setting.distributor_label_singular#] link, and searching for and selecting a new #application.returned_customer_setting.distributor_label_singular#.</cfoutput>
</td></tr>

<tr><td colspan="2">

<strong>Products:</strong><Br>
You can change the products by clicking on the [change products] link, searching for the products you are interested in and selecting them.
<p></p>
<em>Product Values:</em><br>
1. Description: The description of the product.<br
2. Case Cost: The amount the product costs to produce.<br>
3. Case Net Weight (Lbs): The weight of the product per case in pounds.<br>
4. Case List Price: The listed price of a case of the product.<br>
<p></p>
<em>User Entered Values:</em><br>
5. Proposed Case List Price: Enter the price you would like to evaluate for the product.<br>
6. Quantity (Case):  The amount of the product you are proposing to be evaluated.<br>
<p></p>
<em>Calculated Values:</em><br>
7. Volume (Pounds): The quantity you entered (#6) calculated in pounds.<br>
8. Total Cost: The case cost of the Item (#2) multiplied by the quantity (#6).<Br>
9. Revenue: The revenue generated by the proposed price and quantity (#5 x #6).<Br>
10. Mix Percentage of Revenue: This is the percentage of revenue that the product is responsible for. So if there are three items, one of which earns $200, one of which earns $300 and one of which earns $500, the mix percentage would be 20% for the first item, 30% for the second and 50% for the third.<br>
11. Mix Percentage of Weight: The percentage of total weight that the product is responsible for.<br>
12. Extended Margin Dollar Amount: The total margin in dollars is calculated by finding the difference between the Proposed Case List Price and the Case Cost (#5 - #2) and multiplying that by the quantity (#6).<br>
13. Extended Margin Percent: The percent of margin that will be created by the proposed case list price (#5).<br>
<p></p>
<strong>Costs:</strong>
<p></p>
<em>Program Incentive Costs: </em><br>
You can enter incentive costs that will affect the margin for the trade plan you are evaluating. Enter a brief description, the amount, and whether the incentive will be dollars per pound or percentage of revenue.  You can add additional Incentives by clicking on the plus icon, and remove them by clicking on the minus icon.
<p></p>
On the right, you can select whether the incentive applies to a product or not. When you click on the calculate button, you will be able to see the reduction created by each incentive and the total amount of the costs.
<p></p>
<em>Miscellaneous Costs: </em><br>
Miscellaneous costs operate the same way that program incentives do, but are  not related to the incentives - such as spoilage, brokerage and cash discounts.
<p></p>
<em>Profit Analysis:</em><br>
Clicking on the [calculate] link will populate information in the Cost and Profit Analysis areas.
<p></p>
<ul>
<li><em>Program Incentive Costs</em>: The total costs generated by program incentives</li>
<li><em>Miscellaneous Costs:</em> The total miscellaneous costs</li>
<li><em>Item Name:</em> The percentage of margin for each item (original margin minus program and miscellaneous costs).</li>
<li><em>Total Net Margin:</em> The net margin for all items in the program combined.</li>
<li><em>Total Net Profit:</em> The total dollar profit from all items in the trade plan. The Total Net Margin and Profit are surrounded by a box which will be green to indicate a profitable plan and red if the plan will lose money.</li>
</ul>
Clicking on [save] will save the trade plan you have created.
</td></tr>

</table>
